From 85c680c8ab803afc90e9659060230d621ece748f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:52:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] serial: add Baochip bao1x uDMA UART driver and DUART
 earlycon

The bao1x console UART is a PULP-style uDMA UART with an asymmetric
programming model: the transmitter is DMA-only and can fetch solely
from the dedicated IFRAM banks, while the receiver has a PIO path
(VALID/DATA register pair) that raises an "rx char" event per byte.
The driver takes a private IFRAM slice via a second reg entry and
bounces transmit data through it chunk-wise, driven by the "tx done"
event; receive is interrupt-driven PIO. Both events arrive through the
bao1x IRQARRAY bank 5. Console writes transmit synchronously.

The SoC also has a trivial four-register TX-only debug UART (DUART)
that needs no clock or pin configuration; it is exposed as earlycon
only ("earlycon" with stdout-path or earlycon=bao1x_duart) since it
has no receiver.

Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/Kconfig       |  24 ++
 drivers/tty/serial/Makefile      |   2 +
 drivers/tty/serial/bao1x_duart.c |  52 ++++
 drivers/tty/serial/bao1x_uart.c  | 457 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/uapi/linux/serial_core.h |   3 +
 5 files changed, 538 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/tty/serial/bao1x_duart.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/tty/serial/bao1x_uart.c

